@how own mechanism: Build only the minimal linking feature and test it with one or two tightly scoped pilots. (source: this pattern's ! conclusion line; L7 rationale-backfill, zai-1, 2026-09-05)

! conclusion: 
  Build only the minimal linking feature and test it with one or two tightly
  scoped pilots.

  + context: You are defining a tightly scoped build-and-test phase that focuses only on core linking actions, so pilots can answer whether collective sense-making improves with these features. This does not apply when the linking loop is already validated for the

  + IF:
    Budget is small and the linking concept is unproven with real groups.

  + HOWEVER:
    Shipping broader features before testing risks consuming funds without
    answering the central question.
    target cohort.

  + THEN:
    Implement only propose/confirm/view links and run short pilots with carefully
    chosen partners (e.g., ACMi, a university class).

  + BECAUSE:
    Concentrating on the linking loop lets partners judge whether collective
    sense-making improves.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    next[Pick 1–2 partners and co-design a lightweight pilot plan documenting observations.]
    next[Define a decision threshold (e.g., pilots report new shared insights) that gates broader feature build-out.]
